// A mausoleum over a crypt's way down (DUNGEONS.md, *A crypt's mouth*): the churchyard places it
// at its foot, its door to the yard; the dungeon draws it - its walls, roof and way down are the crypt
// entrance part's (dungeonParts/cryptEntrance.json5), whose footprint and door this matches: 30 m
// along its front, 16 m deep, its door 6 m wide 11 m along its front from its middle.
{
  name: "Mausoleum",
  type: "mouth",
  mouth: { width: 30, depth: 16, height: 9, door: [11, 6], wall: 1 },
}
